      "new_ids": [
        "unit.test_state_inspection_rules.EngineEntryInspectionTests.test_engine_entry_checks_presence_and_length_while_check_compares_bytes"
      ],
      "note": "The autospec repository is replaced by the real ResearchRepository on the in-process Git fake, so the state is a stored surface_state and the output row carries its contract field 'path'. The old per-callback checks become port-level ones: no read_objects during the entry inspection, one batch read of every manifest path at the loaded snapshot, and no single-file artifact read. The product answers lengths of artifacts it published itself from memory (repository._known_artifact), so no Git query exists at the first head; the snapshot-retention check (engine.head moved during the queries) is made at the next head, another writer's commit, where the lengths are queried. The 'omit' mode of both batch readers is pinned by outcomes: the removed prompt fails the entry inspection with its own message and check reports 'EX-1: input artifact is missing: prompt' instead of raising.",
      "disposition": "moved"
    },
